// RAW content slot — the counterpart to replacable.tss (the ESCAPED/safe slot).
// For elements whose content is markup/code by NATURE and cannot be escaped as text:
//   - HTML raw-text elements (style/script/iframe, noscript) whose text content
//     serializes VERBATIM — textContent does NOT escape it on SSR, so the safe t:
//     slot gives a false guarantee here;
//   - <template> — an inert markup container (escaping would defeat its purpose);
//   - elements that compose child markup (audio/video <source>/<track>).
// This uses insert's raw h: path: content is NOT escaped and MUST be author-trusted
// (or run through a host sanitize() seam — backlogged). Greppable: `->get @h/rawcontent`.
->inner {
    h: html;
}

->get {
    t: '@h/global.tss';
}
